# hazard-strip: a 2-wide spike strip on the floor with one-way ledges raised on
# each side. The whole course is single-jumpable: hop up a ledge (2 up), jump
# across over the spikes (4 across), land on the far ledge. H stands for a
# hazard tile; the strip sits on the base row's neighbors, so the floor stays intact.
